></circle><path d=\"M248 65 L304 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M248 65 L304 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M436 65 L492 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M436 65 L492 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M582 34 L638 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M582 34 L638 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M436 65 L492 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M436 65 L492 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Handler</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"203\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Bulkhead</text><rect x=\"304\" y=\"43\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"370\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Circuit breaker</text><rect x=\"492\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"537\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Timeout</text><rect x=\"492\" y=\"74\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"537\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Fallback</text><rect x=\"638\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"683\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Search</text></svg><figcaption>Call path with protections</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Liveness probe that checks the database; a DB blip restarts all pods.</li>\n<li>Retry placed at several layers (client, gateway, service) multiplies attempts 3 x 3 x 3.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"decision-gravity","title":"Decision gravity","html":"<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Decision</th>\n<th>Gravity</th>\n<th>Why</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Add AZs / spread pods</td>\n<td>Reversible</td>\n<td>Infra change</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sync replication</td>\n<td>Reversible, but changes write latency contract</td>\n<td>Can relax in an incident</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SLO targets</td>\n<td>Reversible socially, hard politically</td>\n<td>Tighten later is easy, loosening needs agreement</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Circuit breaker / bulkhead config</td>\n<td>Reversible</td>\n<td>Config</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Expand-contract migrations</td>\n<td>Process, not tech</td>\n<td>Makes deploys reversible</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Choosing Patroni vs distributed SQL</td>\n<td><strong>One-way door</strong></td>\n<td>Database engine change is a multi-quarter migration</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Metrics label scheme / tracing format</td>\n<td>Semi-reversible</td>\n<td>Dashboards and alerts depend on names</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying \"we can always roll back\" after a destructive schema change; rollback of code does not roll back data.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"concepts-learned","title":"Concepts learned","html":"<ul>\n<li>Availability math: series vs parallel, nines</li>\n<li>Multi-AZ design, N+1 capacity, cross-AZ latency and cost</li>\n<li>RPO and RTO, sync vs async replication, leader election</li>\n<li>SLI, SLO, error budget, burn-rate alerts</li>\n<li>Timeout, retry budget, circuit breaker, bulkhead, load shedding, graceful degradation</li>\n<li>Canary, blue/green, feature flags, expand-contract migrations</li>\n<li>Metastable failures, observability (metrics, logs, traces) and cardinality</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Stating patterns without saying which failure each one addresses.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Spread everything across 3 AZs at about 60% load per AZ; DB uses a sync standby in another AZ with automatic failover.</li>\n<li>Define SLOs per user journey (reads 99.95%, writes 99.9%), use error budgets to control release speed, alert on burn rate.</li>\n<li>Protect callers with timeouts, budgeted retries, circuit breakers, bulkheads, load shedding and fallbacks.</li>\n<li>Deploy with canaries, feature flags and expand-contract schema changes.</li>\n<li>Reliability adds roughly 40 to 50% cost: about $480k/month at 100M users.</li>\n<li>Next failure domain is the whole region, which Stage 9 tackles.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}